  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically asked about acute red flags, clarified the procedural state (RC2 met), recognized the multi-disease risk (RC3 met), set medication/bowel safety boundaries (RC5 met), and gave an executable follow-up plan (RC6 met). However, the doctor did not actively address the privacy-sensitive viral hepatitis/HBV-DNA information gap when the family hesitated about ‘virus/transmission’ topics; the family disclosed no viral status and the doctor never normalized the need or offered a de-identified pathway, making RC4 (required for decision-critical lab gaps) only partially met. This minor omission caps the grade at 2 Borderline. High-order points HO1-HO4 were either partially addressed or not triggered.",
